      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2003 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "The rotablator burr rarely becomes trapped within calcified lesions. Manual traction can be ineffective and dangerous. We report a case that illustrates a novel technique involving use of a percutaneous snare in conjunction with partial disassembly of the rotablator device to remove a trapped burr without need for open surgical intervention."
      },
